 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "The wind is born again.\nA carpet of white snows, like flowers,\nWhispers in the nightingales' hollow\nLike a fond mistress's bow.\nThere are nights that move without,\nThere are days when storm winds are gentle,\nAnd the bare and cold air heaves softly\nIn their sunny splendour against\nThe moon-minted old windows.\nOn mountains where never\nWas sunshine before - some few hours\nOf sun doth rain us with ever",
